dev.verifyfail=The write was NOT confirmed at offset 0x%s.\nRead through a fresh handle, the device returned the old bytes.\n\nLikely causes:\n- the stick/disk is write-protected (switch or controller);\n- Windows is guarding the sectors of a mounted volume - close the programs\n  using the disk and reopen it;\n- the drive's controller acknowledges writes without storing them (a failing\n  or counterfeit stick) - run Extras -> Write diagnostics;\n- the program is not running as administrator.
